course: dictionary
lesson: 15341
title: Softy: kind or teasing?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and the context tells you which meaning is right. «Softy» is an informal word. It can mean a kind, gentle person who is easily moved. «Grandma is a softy. She always gives us an extra biscuit.» Grandma is not weak. She is kind and gentle with us.
explain: The second meaning is a teasing word for someone who seems too weak or scared. «Stop being such a softy, it's only a little spider!» Here the speaker is teasing someone, so softy means a wimp. Look at the feeling in the sentence: a teasing word can hurt, so be careful how you use it.
explain: Ask yourself what fits. Try swapping in "a gentle person" or "a wimp". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning. The plural is softies, and softie is another spelling of the same word.
fact: «Softy» is an informal word, so you hear it in talk more than in formal writing.
fact: «Softy» can mean a kind, gentle person who is easily moved or who can't be strict.
fact: «Softy» can also be a teasing word for someone thought too weak or scared, a wimp.
fact: The plural is «softies», and «softie» is another spelling.
fact: Teachers may remind pupils not to call others names, even friendly-sounding ones.
exercise: «Dad is a big softy with our puppy.» What does softy mean here? | A strict teacher who never smiles | A fast runner | A type of soft bread | *A gentle person who is easily moved
exercise: Sam laughs, «Don't be such a softy, it's only a little dark!» What does softy mean here? | *Someone too scared, a wimp | A kind person who helps | A soft pillow | A rich person
exercise: Which is the correct plural of softy? | softys | softees | *softies | softy's
test: Which word is closest in meaning to softy, as in a kind, gentle person? | *Kind-hearted | Bully | Cross | Tough
test: Mum said, «Stop calling your brother a softy, that's not kind.» Why did Mum say this? | *Because softy can be a hurtful tease | Because softy is a rude word for a teacher | Because it is a spelling mistake | Because softy means a loud noise
exam: Which sentence uses softy to mean a kind, gentle person? | «The softy bread was stale and hard.» | *«Our neighbour is a softy and always gives the dog a treat.» | «The softy weather made us wear coats.» | «She put the softy sum on the board.»
